###The Agent 365 registry (M365 admin center) is a centralised, tenant-wide inventory of agents; coverage depends on the supported platforms, integrations and registration/discovery mechanisms. The registry list and the agent detail pages expose metadata such as owner, platform/publisher, status, permissions/scopes, data sources, risk signals and usage, but not every field is populated for every agent type. Each Entra agent identity is a service principal (servicePrincipalType 'ServiceIdentity', Graph type #microsoft.graph.agentIdentity) with its own unique directory object ID; it has no app registration of its own - its agentIdentityBlueprintId holds the blueprint's app ID. Registry records can reference the blueprint, agent identity and, where one exists, the optional agent user. The inventory is also exposed through the Microsoft Graph package catalog API (copilot/admin/catalog/packages), which is separate from the Entra agent identity API.
Gaps / caveats: Identity model varies by agent type: Copilot Studio agents created after Agent ID was enabled get an agent identity; agents created earlier (or where the environment had not opted in before July 2026) may still use a classic app registration/service principal, which Microsoft is migrating; Agent Builder (declarative) agents currently have neither an app registration nor an Agent ID, so they appear in the registry/catalog but not as Entra agent identities. No dedicated 'business classification' field was confirmed; custom security attributes on agent identities could hold it (needs design). The Agent 365 Graph APIs require an Agent 365 licence - confirmed in our tenant test on 11-Oct-2026.
