###Microsoft 365 admin center > Agents > Tools lets admins allow/block MCP servers, plugins and skills org-wide; blocking an MCP server also disables dependent plugins and connectors. Developer-registered tools (e.g. remote MCP servers) go to an admin review/approval queue (AI Administrator or Global Administrator). A preview integration with Azure API Management (AI Gateway) discovers MCP servers registered in APIM for governance; per-tool controls need the APIM AI Gateway tier. Conditional Access for agent identities governs token access to Entra-protected resources.
Gaps / caveats: There is no general-purpose egress gateway for all agent traffic to external resources; non-Microsoft destinations need APIM/Global Secure Access designs. Tools governance may not be available in all regions yet, and the APIM integration is preview.
