###Entra Agent ID blocks highly privileged roles for agents (Global Administrator, Privileged Role Administrator, User Administrator) and custom roles cannot be assigned to agent identities. Permissions are granted explicitly (app roles / delegated grants), inheritable permissions are controlled on the blueprint, and Conditional Access for agents can block access by risk. Microsoft best practice is to periodically audit blueprint permissions to avoid privilege creep.
Gaps / caveats: No 'permission boundary' construct (a hard ceiling per agent) was found. Copilot Studio connections can default to the maker's own credentials, so an agent may act with the maker's access (third-party analysis) - needs a design standard. Usage-based right-sizing is not confirmed (see #19).
